Chapter 7
After glancing around the room one last time, I decide to walk over to Miss Moon.
(t): She seems to be the type of person to keep a cool head in these kinds of situations.
(t): And I kind of want to know how this affects work.
As soon as I get a little closer to her, I notice that something is a little weird.
Miss Moon is standing among a group of people and is scanning the room.
(t): It's like she's looking for someone.
The people around her all have a mysterious air about them. I can see exhaustion in all of their eyes, but each one of them is still ridiculously attractive. 
It's kind of intimidating, yet Miss Moon somehow fits right in. I guess she herself is known to be kind of mysterious even in the office.
Seeing that she seems to already be in company, I hesitate and stand still for a moment. Just then my gaze meets hers.
(t): Oh, she's looking at me!
I awkwardly wave in their direction.
(t): Ugh, now that she's seen me, it would be weird to just walk away.
I finally walk over to her entirely, and for a moment I swear I see a hint of panic in her expression. But then she flashes me a polite smile.
Miss Moon: Hello {playerName}. I'm glad to see you also made it to safety.
(t): Did I just imagine that?
Me: Yeah, same here. That was really scary, right?
Miss Moon just nods.
I feel like some of the group are staring at me a little too much.
Me: Uh … am I interrupting you?
I tilt my head and look at the group behind Miss Moon, but before I could meet their gaze, they all avoid eye contact.
(t): Why are they acting like this? How suspicious.
Miss Moon: No, of course not. Please excuse them, they are not used to meeting my acquaintances.
I try to joke around a bit to lift the mood.
Me: Oh my, is it your family? Am I the first employee to meet them?
Miss Moon looks kind of uncomfortable but she keeps it professional.
Miss Moon: They're not— … well, I guess they're similar to family, so you're not entirely wrong. I try to keep my personal life and business separate as strictly as possible.
(t): As always. I always manage to miss the mark.
Me: Haha … right. Then I won't pry any further, ahem. May I ask about what will happen to work? Will we get a vacat—?
I try to change the topic to something work-related to avoid any more awkwardness, but then I get interrupted.
???: Boss, I found everyone!
A group of three young men appear and walk up to us.
(t): Boss? Does Miss Moon have multiple businesses?
I look at her and almost let out a gasp. Her expression is a mix of anger and despair as she directs her sharp gaze at the three men.
(t): Yep. Miss Moon is probably the scariest person I know. I wonder what's wrong.
One of the men nudges the one that called out to Miss Moon with his elbow.
He then sees me, and I see how his face changes from happy to flustered.
???: Oh, uh … Sorry, wrong person.
They try to make a swift exit, but then Miss Moon speaks up.
Miss Moon: You three. Join the others. I will have a talk with you later.
Her voice isn't particularly loud, but it still causes everyone in the group to hold their breath in fear. Including me.
It gives me the chills while also reminding me that Miss Moon is a very strict boss that nobody wants to get in trouble with.
Miss Moon: Apologies {playerName}. I must speak with my family now. I will see you at work in two days. I assure you that, if the office were destroyed today, I will have found a solution to continue work by then.
CHOICE OPTION 1: Wait, just two days?
(t): I knew that hoping for a real vacation was wishful thinking on my part, but TWO DAYS?! What about the employees' physical and mental wellbeing, boss???
Me: Miss Moon! Please excuse my rudeness, but don't you think that might be a bit too early, considering we're dealing with a natural disaster here?
(t): Oops!
It occurred to me then that I might anger this already agitated boss of mine even more.
I peek up at her only to see her coldly staring down at me.
Her eyes are two different colours, but both express an icy yet blazing kind of authority.
Miss Moon: Already thinking of slacking off again?
(t): I've made a mistake.
I feel the cold sweat dripping down my back.
I gulp audibly.
Me: I'm sorry, Miss Moon. I promise to do better in the future.
Miss Moon: That's what I thought. Now off you go.
Me: Yes, Ma'am!
I hurriedly get away from her and her supposed family.
CHOICE OPTION 2: Right, it was a pleasure. Bye!
(t): Yes! This is the perfect opportunity to get out of this uncomfortable environment.
I decide to remove myself from this situation as swiftly as possible.
Me: Right then, if I can help with anything, please let me know. Now if you'll excuse me.
She just nods curtly and turns to the people she called her family.
(t): It is a little weird though. They don't really seem like a real family. The vibes are a bit off. And that man earlier called her ‘Boss'…
(t): Whatever, I shouldn't assume things about another's familial situation. Let's just get out of here.
I walk away without looking back, scared that I would have to meet their mysterious gazes again.
CHOICE OPTION 3: Um, is everything alright?
I feel like it's my fault the mood turned sour.
Me: Um, is everything alright?
Miss Moon: Yes, this does not concern you, so you needn't worry. Please just ignore it. I will send an email to all employees regarding work as soon as we get out of this bunker.
(t): I don't want to just leave her like this though. I haven't even introduced myself to her family.
Me: I apologise. If I've offended anyone, I would like to—
Miss Moon: Enough! As I've mentioned before, I hate to mix business with personal matters. I have nothing work-related to discuss with you anymore. I will see you at work soon.
(t): I was just trying to fix things … Why is she so hostile?
Me: Alright, I understand. Have a nice day, everyone.
And with that I distance myself from my boss and the rest of them.
(t): I guess it's my fault for trying to mind someone else's business when I'm not in the place to do so.
But the way Miss Moon spoke to me kind of hurt. I was hoping we could maybe get a little closer today, but maybe it's still too early for that.
CONTINUE HERE AFTER CHOICE OPTIONS
(t): Well, I'm sure it will get better the more time we spend together at the company. I just hope we can have a more comfortable and light atmosphere at work soon.
I try to get these thoughts out of my head, but there is a weird, indescribable feeling that lingers in my chest.
Soon enough, after some hours have passed, the bunker door opens, and we learn that the earthquake is officially over and it's safe for us to return to the surface again.
Luckily there were only a few injuries and no casualties. The buildings are not in very good condition, so they open up a temporary shelter area with lots of tents for the affected people.
My apartment complex stayed intact, and I'm relieved that I can just go home and get some rest now.
Or so I thought.
When I enter my apartment, I am met with a grandiose chaos.
The walls may be sturdy enough to withstand an earthquake but some of my belongings need to be replaced.
(t): My poor TV!
I see my TV, among other fragile items, in shambles on the floor.
(t): Oh, but I'm way too tired to clean up right now.
I decide to dedicate tomorrow to tidying everything up and just free my bed from all the rubbish so I can finally rest.
As soon as I close my eyes, I drift into a deep sleep and forget all the ruckus for one night.